  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nThis afternoon, showers and thunderstorms have popped up along\nthe sea breeze and some residual differential heating boundaries\nfrom earlier cloud cover. Some convection has been accompanied \nby frequent lightning and heavier showers but the vast majority \nof the activity is expected to stay sub severe this afternoon. \nShort term models have shower and thunderstorm activity \ndecreasing through the evening and ceasing around 00z.\n\nTaking a wider view for the upcoming period, an upper ridge and\nBermuda high pressure will be centered off the coast through \nSaturday, becoming suppressed late in the weekend as shortwave \nenergy pushes across the mid- Atlantic. More of a zonal pattern\ndevelops next week with a series of shortwave troughs pushing \nacross the area. Precip chances will be near climo each day with\nwidely scattered showers and thunderstorms developing each \nafternoon, then dissipating with loss of heating during the \nevening. The severe threat appears minimal through the period \nwith limited shear and forcing. \n\nA gradual warming trend will continue through the period as well\nwith highs in the lower 90s inland through the weekend, then\nwarming in to the mid 90s next week. Temps generally in the mid\nto upper 80s along the coast. The probabilities for Major Heat\nRisk increase to around 60-80% Monday through Thursday of next\nweek.",
